},"signature":"{\"payload\": \"\", \"payloadType\": \"application/vnd.rebar.authorship.v1+json\", \"signatures\": [{\"keyid\": \"594c-9dcf-5ad6-4e6d\", \"sig\": \"\"}]}","signer_pubkey":"ssh-ed25519 AAAAC3NzaC1lZDI1NTE5AAAAIHe3p+OG3L79IIh99qRBEkAEXaU+VbeQcSfhIu4M2F8b rebar-bot joeoakhart+bot@navapbc.com"},{"content_hash":"4de81e42382b4ab1c28dca33b9717826bf00263297e8890b64d3fd7bf29f7d0a","event_uuid":"17da38e3-19ba-40f4-ba8a-8e1f95cbfa14","position":{"commit_sha":"106f08e3573942421e8c7ff960338833d043d2a7","position":"1786207480573223001-17da38e3-19ba-40f4-ba8a-8e1f95cbfa14"},"signature":"{\"payload\": \"\", \"payloadType\": \"application/vnd.rebar.authorship.v1+json\", \"signatures\": [{\"keyid\": \"594c-9dcf-5ad6-4e6d\", \"sig\": \"\"}]}","signer_pubkey":"ssh-ed25519 AAAAC3NzaC1lZDI1NTE5AAAAIHe3p+OG3L79IIh99qRBEkAEXaU+VbeQcSfhIu4M2F8b rebar-bot joeoakhart+bot@navapbc.com"}],"bridge_alerts":[],"claim_harness":null,"claim_remote_session":null,"claimed_session":null,"comments":[{"author":"RebarBotNava","author_email":"joeoakhart+bot@navapbc.com","author_id":"594c-9dcf-5ad6-4e6d","body":"Plan inventory corrected for an existing anti-migration guard: tests/unit/test_canary_bridge_wiring.py::test_flush_cas_loop_stays_in_yaml_verbatim_shape must be rewritten in the cutover change, not merely allowed to fail. It will pin the new single push-only strict canary step, synchronous override, absence of inline CAS/raw git, preserved red disposition, and updated file-level rationale.","timestamp":1786147905202013001},{"author":"RebarBotNava","author_email":"joeoakhart+bot@navapbc.com","author_id":"594c-9dcf-5ad6-4e6d","body":"Plan-review remediation: expanded both workflow invocations to the complete argparse-valid shapes (`--tracker .`, reconciler `--message`, `--author-name`, and `--author-email`), split the escaped acceptance-criteria lines, explicitly covered the stale sibling rationale in `test_no_logic_bearing_rebar_calls_left_in_yaml`, and added the two merge-command-dependent workflow tests discovered by exact-command grep. File impact now includes both newly identified test files. The interrupted review had validated these as the grounded defects; rerunning from the corrected material.","timestamp":1786164930261090001},{"author":"RebarBotNava","author_email":"joeoakhart+bot@navapbc.com","author_id":"594c-9dcf-5ad6-4e6d","body":"TDD contract card and parity census for 742d:\n\n- authoritative_contract: ticket ACs plus current workflow red-on-persistent-failure behavior and the landed private CLI in src/rebar/_store/push.py.\n- trigger_preconditions: reconciler exact run block starts with a dirty real tracker under project sync.push=off; canary exact run block starts clean but one commit ahead; strict-failure cases use a real bare origin with a rejecting pre-receive hook.\n- production_path: parse each named GitHub Actions step, substitute only the run-id expression, and execute the exact shell with the worktree venv against real temporary git repositories.\n- test_tier: executable workflow subprocess + real git refs; a source-only assertion is one tier too low because it cannot prove argparse, env, commit identity, delivery, exit code, or pending-commit behavior.\n- observable_postcondition: reconciler exits 0, pushes the dirty event, and the remote commit has the exact subject and supplied author despite sync.push=off; rejection exits nonzero and keeps the local commit. Canary pushes an ahead commit; policy rejection exits nonzero and keeps it pending.\n- collateral_invariants: unrelated files and remote history remain intact; no empty commit; working tree clean after successful reconciler commit; rejected local commit remains reachable.\n- negative_control: project sync.push=off without the workflow's REBAR_SYNC_PUSH=always would not deliver; the exact block must override it.\n- recovery/contention: no new retry implementation is introduced; both calls ride the already-locked core seam, so existing in-process push suites own rejection→fetch→merge→re-push contention. No new contention harness is warranted.\n- ci_gate: exact nodes collected/executed under make test; focused run first, then make lint/typecheck/test.\n\nSurface parity: CLI/private process boundary = in scope through both exact workflow blocks; automated callers = in scope, one executable test per workflow; library facade = out of scope/no contract change, existing best-effort tests retained; MCP/API = out of scope/no call-path change; dual-direction/inbound Jira application = out of scope because this cutover changes only outbound tickets delivery.","timestamp":1786166249784384001},{"author":"RebarBotNava","author_email":"joeoakhart+bot@navapbc.com","author_id":"594c-9dcf-5ad6-4e6d","body":"Pushed Gerrit change 1538 (e462f811, Change-Id Ia8b5fcb6fc89703390b2b1eb57d324f00436d59e). Before push: fetched origin, rebased onto origin/main (no-op), proved 0 behind / 1 ahead, then reran 47 affected tests, lint/actionlint, typecheck, and diff check green. Held-out real-git workflow oracle passed 2/2 and rejected strict/authorship mutations. Waiting for independent LLM-Review +1 and Verified +1 before submit.","timestamp":1786167236384641001},{"author":"RebarBotNava","author_email":"joeoakhart+bot@navapbc.com","author_id":"594c-9dcf-5ad6-4e6d","body":"Landed as Gerrit change 1538, commit 11a026540b on origin/main. Gate evidence: LLM-Review +1; Verified +1 from GitHub run 31241954882; zero unresolved comments. TDD evidence: six contract nodes RED before implementation; implementer saw four happy-path nodes only; two executable real-git workflow tests were physically held out and passed 2/2 on first restore; mutations removing canary --strict and reconciler --author-email each made the held-out oracle RED; affected suite passed 47 tests plus lint/actionlint and typecheck. Full CI passed across all matrices and integration tiers.","timestamp":1786168472776133001},{"author":"RebarBotNava","author_email":"joeoakhart+bot@navapbc.com","author_id":"594c-9dcf-5ad6-4e6d","body":"Completion-verifier remediation evidence: the reconciler standing-decision block at .github/workflows/reconcile-bridge.yml lines 25-31 now states that the final strict core adapter commits when needed and synchronously pushes dirty or clean-ahead state, keeping the workflow red on failure. The canary standing-decision block at .github/workflows/reconcile-bridge-canary.yml lines 14-19 already states that the strict synchronous adapter delegates CAS recovery to rebar._store.push. scripts/canary_bridge.py lines 1-5 and tests/unit/test_canary_bridge_wiring.py lines 1-12, 63-98 document and enforce the same reversal. External gate evidence for the [operator-attested] test criterion remains CI run 31241954882: focused workflow coverage, lint/actionlint, typecheck, default suites, and integration suites all passed across the full matrix.","timestamp":1786168998761520001},{"author":"RebarBotNava","author_email":"joeoakhart+bot@navapbc.com","author_id":"594c-9dcf-5ad6-4e6d","body":"Verifier-driven follow-up pushed as Gerrit change 1540 (commit e8a3874, Change-Id retained by hook). It corrects the reconciler standing-decision block that still claimed the engine never pushes. Before push: fetched origin, rebased onto origin/main, proved 0 behind / 1 ahead, then reran the 16 focused workflow tests, lint/actionlint, and diff check green. Awaiting LLM-Review +1 and Verified +1; ticket remains in progress.","timestamp":1786169095483486001},{"author":"RebarBotNava","author_email":"joeoakhart+bot@navapbc.com","author_id":"594c-9dcf-5ad6-4e6d","body":"Verifier follow-up landed as Gerrit change 1540, commit 039fe7bbde on origin/main. Gate evidence: LLM-Review +1, Verified +1 from CI run 31243115851, and zero unresolved comments. The reconciler and canary standing-decision blocks now both describe strict synchronous core-owned delivery; focused 16-test workflow oracle and lint/actionlint passed locally after the mandatory origin/main refresh.","timestamp":1786170300725928001},{"author":"RebarBotNava","author_email":"joeoakhart+bot@navapbc.com","author_id":"594c-9dcf-5ad6-4e6d","body":"Execution-phase review found the final stale synthetic raw-git exemption rationale. Remediated the ticket into a post-land closeout plan and pushed the one-line cleanup as Gerrit change 1541 (e04c0e69ab). Before push: fetched/rebased origin/main, proved 0 behind / 1 ahead, then 46 focused tests, lint/actionlint, and commit-hook mypy passed. Awaiting LLM-Review +1 and Verified +1; no force close.","timestamp":1786171482070659001},{"author":"RebarBotNava","author_email":"joeoakhart+bot@navapbc.com","author_id":"594c-9dcf-5ad6-4e6d","body":"Gerrit 1541 CI rerun 31266912051 remained non-real: py3.11 repeated known flake fade-ea90-7564-4715 (gw3 crash in test_matching_guard_is_accepted after 11,435 passes); py3.12 exposed a separate temp-fixture git merge conflict after 11,434 passes, filed as cb9c-49cb-5aba-488d and linked discovered_from. The one-line raw-git fixture-comment change cannot affect either test. Other matrices/gates passed; posting another recheck, never bypassing Verified.","timestamp":1786207480573223001}],"created_at":1786142486742185001,"creation_channel":"cli","deps":[{"link_uuid":"ad97ac7e-3273-4695-866d-b100d9633851","relation":"depends_on","target_id":"2bc9-75aa-a08a-478a"},{"link_uuid":"3b895837-aaa7-4161-921c-0d6de841cfaf","relation":"relates_to","target_id":"266d-dd93-01b6-4d5f"},{"link_uuid":"be16e163-2430-4c72-a4b4-01bc6945db9a","relation":"relates_to","target_id":"6318-7e48-c879-478a"},{"link_uuid":"bdee25fa-5f0e-446c-b166-0ba7ca3bc017","relation":"relates_to","target_id":"a576-a4db-ae47-4a10"},{"link_uuid":"64c038d3-93e8-4cc3-9237-e84e3324a574","relation":"relates_to","target_id":"4dc0-731b-be37-40f8"}],"description":"## Completion state\n\nThis ticket is in execution-phase closeout. The migration landed in Gerrit change 1538 (origin/main 11a026540b), and the standing-decision correction landed in change 1540 (origin/main 039fe7bbde). One final stale synthetic exemption rationale remains in tests/unit/test_raw_git_write_lint.py; replace its overturned ticket-4c4f wording with a generic reviewed-fixture rationale and land that documentation-only cleanup through Gerrit.\n\nThe current tree is the intended post-migration state: both workflow-local CAS loops are absent; the reconciler invokes strict synchronous commit-and-push with exact bot identity and subject; the canary invokes strict synchronous push-only delivery; library/MCP best-effort defaults remain unchanged. Copied-template refresh, timing, and no-cleanup rollback are documented.\n\n## Verification\n\n- Run the focused workflow and raw-git lint tests, then make lint.\n- Before Gerrit push, fetch origin, rebase onto origin/main, prove zero behind, and rerun the focused gates.\n- Close only after LLM-Review +1, Verified +1, zero unresolved comments, merge, and completion verification.\n\n## Acceptance Criteria\n\n- [x] Both inline YAML CAS loops are absent and each workflow invokes one complete core push action.\n- [x] Strict synchronous workflow delivery preserves red failure while library/MCP retain best-effort defaults.\n- [x] Reconciler identity and exact commit subject are preserved.\n- [x] The reconciler raw-git exemption is removed.\n- [x] Standing decisions and executable tests document and enforce core ownership.\n- [x] Exactly two real-git workflow smoke tests preserve success and red-failure outcomes.\n- [x] Copied-template migration, timing, and rollback continuity are documented.\n- [x] The overturned decision and landed evidence are recorded on 4c4f-e554-849a-4dfd.\n- [ ] The stale synthetic raw-git exemption rationale no longer claims ticket 4c4f keeps the CAS loop in YAML.\n- [x] [operator-attested] Changes 1538 and 1540 passed both Gerrit votes, zero unresolved comments, and full CI.","env_id":"ade0f2ef-51cc-45a2-bb97-c09846cd3df5","file_impact":[{"path":".github/workflows/reconcile-bridge.yml","reason":"replace dirty commit-back CAS loop with strict core entrypoint and preserve bot identity"},{"path":".github/workflows/reconcile-bridge-canary.yml","reason":"replace client-template flush loop with synchronous strict core call while preserving red disposition"},{"path":"scripts/canary_bridge.py","reason":"update obsolete standing decision that prohibited core ownership"},{"path":"tests/scripts/test_reconcile_bridge_push_retry.py","reason":"replace YAML-loop extraction with executable workflow-block continuity tests"},{"path":"tests/unit/test_canary_bridge_wiring.py","reason":"update anti-migration assertions and both stale rationales for core-owned push"},{"path":"tests/interfaces/store/test_reconcile_workflow_no_shallow_rebase.py","reason":"retire YAML-local merge assertion removed with both inline CAS loops"},{"path":"tests/unit/workflow/test_reconcile_workflow_lint.py","reason":"preserve merge-driver ordering contract without requiring a canary YAML-local merge"},{"path":"CHANGELOG.md","reason":"document copied canary-template shape and refresh action"},{"path":"docs/jira-sync-setup.md","reason":"document opt-in migration and no-cleanup rollback for existing copied workflows"}],"file_impact_scope":"paths","keyring":[],"last_status_env_id":"ade0f2ef-51cc-45a2-bb97-c09846cd3df5","managed_refs":[["depends_on","2bc9-75aa-a08a-478a"],["parent","1c1b-1da2-7ff4-4770"],["relates_to","266d-dd93-01b6-4d5f"],["relates_to","4dc0-731b-be37-40f8"],["relates_to","6318-7e48-c879-478a"],["relates_to","a576-a4db-ae47-4a10"]],"no_file_impact_reason":"","parent_id":"1c1b-1da2-7ff4-4770","parent_status_uuid":"b7e3ac30-40bf-473b-874c-730cc88a8c87","plan_review_phase":"execution","preconditions_summary":{"status":"pre-manifest"},"priority":1,"reverts":[],"status":"in_progress","tags":["bridge","ci","workflow"],"ticket_id":"742d-54f1-3b6f-4864","ticket_type":"task","title":"Migrate both bridge workflows to core push entrypoints","verify_commands":[]},"source_event_uuids":["74eb2ba8